@misc{antoine2026loss, title = {On the loss landscape of the linear neural network: beyond critical points}, author = {Lejay, Antoine and Lenotre, Lionel and Toubra, Sa\{ï\}d}, year = {2026}, eprint = {2611.26671}, archivePrefix = {arXiv}, url = {https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.26671} }
Identifies and characterizes 'channels to infinity' in neural loss landscapes where weights diverge but loss decreases. ... Establishes error bounds and linear convergence for the regularized loss of deep linear networks.
A survey of gradient flow dynamics and loss landscape properties for deep linear neural networks.
The present article introduces an intermediate structure, termed the critical thalweg, which encompasses all critical points and exhibits key geometric properties. Beyond providing a geometric proof of Baldi \& Hornik's results using simpler assumptions than the existing literature, this framework offers a global view of the loss landscape that can be easily visualized in a two-dimensional plane.

